{#- Reference box (Notes-Transfer-Help-Publish · 21 Oct 2026). One shape for "your reference" wherever
    it appears, so the reader learns it once; Share-Copy-3's "Reference a1b2c3d4" copies it. Styles: notes.css
    "Reference box". Gold + muted only (suite rule: no status colours, no syntax colours). Made-up
    characters only: never a real transfer id, and the key part is a blur, never real text.
    Usage: {% from "ref-box.njk" import refBox %}{{ refBox("1a2b3c4d", "-5e6f-…") }} -#}
{% macro refBox(ref, rest, refLabel="your reference", keyLabel="the key, never send this") %}
<figure class="ref-box">
  <p class="ref-link" role="img" aria-label="A Share link: share.refueler.io/?uuid= then {{ ref }}, which is {{ refLabel }}, then the rest of the id, then a hash sign and the key, hidden here: {{ keyLabel }}.">
    <span class="ref-muted">share.refueler.io/?uuid=</span><span class="ref-seg"><span class="ref-code">{{ ref }}</span><span class="ref-label">{{ refLabel }}</span></span><span class="ref-muted">{{ rest }}</span><span class="ref-seg ref-key"><span class="ref-hash">#</span><span class="ref-blur">k4Rw9Tq2Lm7Xv0Bc5Nz8Hj3Yp6Ds1Fg</span><span class="ref-label">{{ keyLabel }}</span></span>
  </p>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}
